---
description: Arabic/English i18n and RTL rules
globs: src/app/**/*.{ts,html,scss}, public/i18n/**
alwaysApply: true
---

# i18n / RTL

- Use ngx-translate for all user-facing strings — no hardcoded UI copy
- Keys: `feature.section.key` (e.g. `auth.login.title`)
- Map API ProblemDetails `message.en` / `message.ar` (or messageKey) via translate
- Bilingual DTOs: display with `LanguageService.pick(ar, en)` (`nameAr` / `nameEn`, `arabicName` / `englishName`, `title.ar` / `title.en`).
  NOT a pipe: a pure pipe memoises on its arguments so it would not re-run on a language
  switch, and impure pipes run every CD cycle. Called from a template, `pick()` reads the
  language signal inside a reactive consumer and tracks correctly.
- Runtime-built keys (`permissions.apps.<applicationKey>`, `permissions.groups.<resource>`,
  `myAccess.apps.<module>`) must go through `LanguageService.labelOr(key, fallback)` so an
  API value with no catalogue entry degrades to something readable instead of a raw key
- `LanguageService` sets `document.documentElement.lang` and `dir` (`rtl` for `ar`, `ltr` for `en`)
- Send `Accept-Language` on every HTTP request
- SCSS: prefer logical properties; add `[dir='rtl']` overrides only when needed
- Forms and error panels must flip correctly in both languages
